  urldate = {2026-03-07},
  abstract = {Let G be a finite simple connected graph on [n] and R = K[x1, . . . , xn] the polynomial ring in n variables over a field K. The edge ideal of G is the ideal I(G) of R which is generated by those monomials xixj for which \textbraceleft i, j\textbraceright{} is an edge of G. In the present paper, the possible tuples (n, depth(R/I(G)), reg(R/I(G)), dim R/I(G), deg h(R/I(G))), where deg h(R/I(G)) is the degree of the h-polynomial of R/I(G), arising from Cameron--Walker graphs on [n] will be completely determined.},
